course: dictionary
lesson: 15359
title: Somnambulist: the sleepwalker's word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A somnambulist is a person who walks in their sleep. Take the word apart and you can see the meaning: it comes from Latin, where somnus means sleep and ambulare means to walk. «Last night the somnambulist walked down the hall and into the kitchen, but she was still fast asleep.»
explain: Look for clues in the sentence. «Sam got up in the night, poured himself a glass of milk, and in the morning he had no memory of it.» Sam was asleep the whole time, so he must be a somnambulist. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? A sleepwalker fits, so that is the meaning.
explain: Writers sometimes use the word in a different way. «She moved like a somnambulist, slow and dreamy, not really seeing the room.» Here the word describes how someone moves: slowly and without being fully aware of what they are doing.
fact: A somnambulist is a sleepwalker.
fact: Sleepwalking is common in children and is usually harmless; most children grow out of it.
fact: If you find a somnambulist, gently guide them back to bed.
fact: Keep doors and stairs safe, so a sleepwalker cannot fall or wander outside.
fact: «Somnambulist» comes from Latin somnus (sleep) and ambulare (to walk).
exercise: «The somnambulist walked down the stairs with her eyes shut.» What is a somnambulist? | A very tall tree | A person who sings in the bath | A kind of cloud | *A person who walks in their sleep
exercise: The word somnambulist comes from the Latin word somnus. What does somnus mean? | Walk | *Sleep | Dark | Bed
exercise: Mum said, «Gently guide him back to bed, and check the stairs gate is shut.» Why is the stairs gate important? | It keeps the house warm in winter | *It keeps a sleepwalker from falling down the stairs | It stops visitors from ringing the bell | It keeps the cat from coming in
test: «Sam walked to the kitchen and poured milk, but he was fast asleep and remembered nothing in the morning.» Sam is a what? | A goalkeeper | *A somnambulist | A baker | A pilot
test: Sleepwalking is common in children and usually ___, and most children grow out of it. | painful | contagious | dangerous | *harmless
exam: Writers say someone moved «like a somnambulist». What does this suggest? | Very quickly and loudly | *Slowly and not fully aware of what they are doing | Angrily, shouting at everyone | Happily, dancing in the street
